{"type":"message","id":"3d99d334","parentId":"2b9588ad","timestamp":"2026-05-17T23:02:21.673Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The send endpoint uses Bearer auth. Let me check if the issue is with the API key format. Let me try with the exact same format used for the GET requests. I used -H \"X-API-Key: ...\" for GET requests successfully, but it seems the POST requires \"Authorization: Bearer\". But that gave Unauthorized. \n\nLet me try X-API-Key for POST too.\n\nWait, for GET I used X-API-Key and it worked. For POST it failed with 1101. The 1101 might be a different error. Let me try just the X-API-Key header for POST as well.\n\nActually, wait - looking more carefully at the GET results. They DID work with `X-API-Key`, not `Authorization: Bearer`. \n\nSo X-API-Key worked for the GET requests. Now I'll test that same header approach on the POST endpoint.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-7ec4e7f7-6b55-41f1-ac83-91cceb4a1282","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"**[Heartbeat 23:00 UTC]**\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":19757,"output":277,"cacheRead":112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20146,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779058930963,"responseId":"chatcmpl-7af0bb24-5dca-4773-a4e0-5d9729a86333"}}
